# Copy to .env only if you want to change the defaults.
# The stack runs without this file.

# --- Self-signed (default) ---------------------------------------------------
# Equivalent to:
#
#   SITE_ADDRESS=:443
#   TLS_ARGS=/certs/tls.crt /certs/tls.key
#
# ":443" answers on any hostname or address, and cert-init generates the
# certificate before Caddy starts. The browser warns once because the
# certificate is self-signed; clicking through grants a secure context, which
# is all WebGPU needs.
#
# Browsers match on subjectAltName, so list every address you actually browse
# to. localhost and 127.0.0.1 are always included. Changing this after the
# first run has no effect until you delete the "certs" volume, since
# cert-init deliberately does not overwrite an existing certificate:
#
#   docker compose down && docker volume rm <project>_certs && docker compose up -d
#
# CERT_HOSTS=10.0.0.5,ntlmrain.lan

# --- Let's Encrypt (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment both. SITE_ADDRESS must be a domain that resolves to this host,
# and port 80 must be reachable from the internet for the HTTP-01 challenge.
# Passing an email to Caddy's `tls` directive is what switches it from the
# generated files to ACME.
#
# SITE_ADDRESS=ntlmrain.example.com
# TLS_ARGS=you@example.com
